                <head>No. 1323<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On April 17, 1954, General Muhammad Naguib
                     resigned as Prime Minister of Egypt and was replaced by Colonel
                        Gamal Abdul Nasir, who retained his
                    chairmanship of the Revolutionary Command Council. General Naguib remained President of Egypt until
                    November 15, 1954.</p>
            </div>
